## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design end-to-end tests for multi-region, multi-tenant feature flags, covering UI, API, and background workers, with rapid toggling and race conditions. Demonstrates seeds, isolation strategies, and SLA verification.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flag precedence and propagation across layers
- Cross-region consistency (UI, API, workers)
- Concurrency, load testing, and idempotency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test scaffold for E2E feature-flag toggles
async function testFlagToggle(tenantId, flagKey, value) {
  await api.setFlag(tenantId, flagKey, value);
  await wait(50);
  const uiState = await ui.getFlagState(tenantId, flagKey);
  const workerState = await worker.getFlagState(tenantId, flagKey);
  if (uiState !== value || workerState !== value) throw new Error('Inconsistent state');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure cross-region propagation latency? 
- How do you handle partial failures (region down) and ensure eventual consistency?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical E2E test craft for user onboarding, focusing on external service mocks, data isolation, and idempotent behavior—key in fintech onboarding.

## Key Concepts

- E2E testing of authentication flows
- Mocking external email gateways
- Test data seeding and isolation
- Token expiry and single-use guarantees
- Deterministic assertions across browsers

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example (Cypress)
describe('Email verification onboarding', () => {
  it('activates user via one-time link and prevents reuse', () => {
    cy.request('POST', '/api/signup', { email: 'a@example.com', password: 'P@ssw0rd' })
    .then(() => {
      cy.task('getVerificationLink', 'a@example.com').then(link => {
        cy.visit(link);
        cy.get('#status').should('contain', 'Active');
        cy.visit(link); // reuse attempt
        cy.get('#error').should('exist');
      });
    });
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

